      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input-review",
      "description": "Native review input; retains the inherited review-specific placeholder and green caret as observed drift.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-field-label\">Replacement value<input class=\"ds-field\" placeholder=\"Replacement value\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-field-label{display:grid;gap:6px;font:14px/1.6 var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);color:#354e70}.ds-field{min-width:0;max-width:100%;border:1px solid #bac9dc;border-radius:var(--radius,6px);padding:10px 12px;font:14px var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);color:var(--ink,#182b43);background:white;caret-color:#216646}.ds-field::placeholder{color:#60746a;opacity:1}.ds-field:focus{border-color:#7395d3}.ds-field:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #83a9f1;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rail Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navigation-item",
      "description": "Native navigation button with SVG; active state shown. Compact horizontal layout begins at 800px in the application shell.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\" aria-label=\"Primary navigation\"><button class=\"ds-nav ds-nav-active\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 9h18M3 14h18M9 4v16\"/></svg>Explore</button><button class=\"ds-nav\">Review</button><button class=\"ds-nav\" disabled>Report</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{display:grid;gap:5px;background:var(--rail,#172d4b);padding:16px}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;width:100%;min-height:46px;padding:11px 12px;border:0;border-radius:var(--radius,6px);background:transparent;text-align:left;color:#c1d0e5;font:600 15px var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);cursor:pointer}.ds-nav svg{width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.ds-nav:hover{background:#233c5d;color:white}.ds-nav.ds-nav-active{background:#2b4c79;color:white}.ds-nav:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #83a9f1;outline-offset:3px}.ds-nav:disabled{color:#a8bad4;opacity:1;cursor:not-allowed}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Badges",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "status-neutral",
      "description": "Noninteractive neutral, warning, and success visual variants; text defines the actual application meaning.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-badges\"><span class=\"ds-badge\">Original</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-warning\">Unresolved</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-success\">Approved</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-badges{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.ds-badge{border-radius:4px;font:600 12px var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);padding:4px 8px;background:#edf1f7;color:#4b5f7b}.ds-warning{color:#765019;background:var(--amber-bg,#fff4df)}.ds-success{color:#1f6448;background:#e8f6ee}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Workspace Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "workspace-card",
      "description": "Flat white native section for contextual analytical content.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-card\"><h2>Give the copilot context</h2><p>Describe what the data measures to improve subsequent suggestions.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-card{margin:22px 0;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--line,#d9e1eb);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel,#ffffff);color:var(--ink,#182b43);font:15px/1.5 var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif)}.ds-card h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600}.ds-card p{color:var(--muted,#52647a);font-size:14px;line-height:1.6}@media(max-width:560px){.ds-card{padding:18px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "SVG Finding Marker",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Potential-outlier category marker; exact SVG path data from sheetSvgIcon. Category encoding is not a severity verdict.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-finding\" aria-label=\"Potential outlier, 3 flagged cells\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"16\" r=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"13\" r=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\"/></svg><small>3</small></button>",
      "css": ".ds-finding{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:2px;min-width:24px;height:26px;padding:2px 4px;border:1px solid #7544a7;border-radius:6px;background:#f3edfa;color:#7544a7;font:700 14px var(--font-ui,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);cursor:pointer}.ds-finding svg{width:16px;height:16px;flex-shrink:0;vertical-align:middle}.ds-finding small{margin-left:2px;font-size:10px}.ds-finding:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7544a7;outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Analytical Review Desk",
    "overview": "ClearData is a precise, daylight analytical workspace. An ink-navy navigation rail frames white task surfaces on cool paper; blue identifies actions and selection, green marks final approval, and amber calls attention to exceptions. The character is restrained and information-led: readable data, aligned labels, compact controls, and meaningful hairline divisions.\n\nThe system uses native browser controls, inline SVG icons, and a self-hosted typeface. Dataset evidence remains visually distinct from interpretation and approval. Review content stays in document flow, including its static, unobstructed action footer.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy navigation, white task surfaces, and cool-paper surroundings.",
      "Source Sans 3 with tabular numerals for analytical comparisons.",
      "Blue progression, green final approval, and amber contextual warnings.",
      "Restrained corners, hairline divisions, and SVG finding icons.",
      "Native controls and a static review footer."
    ],
    "rules": [
      { "name": "The Meaning Before Color Rule", "body": "Pair semantic color with visible labels, icons, counts, or evidence; a flagged value is a finding for review, not proof that it is invalid.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Flow First Rule", "body": "Keep the guided action footer static and unobstructed; scrolling evidence and exceptions must not be covered by approval controls.", "section": "elevation" }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use Source Sans 3 and tabular numerals for analytical data.",
      "Do use blue for progression and selection, green for final guided approval, and amber for contextual exceptions.",
      "Do pair finding colors with SVG icons and textual descriptions.",
      "Do preserve common bins and scales in original/working/proposed comparisons.",
      "Do keep the review footer static, after the evidence and exceptions.",
      "Do account for inherited responsive rules when extending the final visual layer."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't infer a dark theme from the navy navigation rail.",
      "Don't equate a finding color with invalid data or automatic treatment.",
      "Don't replace SVG finding icons with glyph icons or raster images.",
      "Don't promote residual legacy fonts, kickers, or green-selection styling into new system rules.",
      "Don't treat documentation completion as the pending finish-review verdict or as Playwright verification."
    ]
  }
}
